==English==

===Etymology===
1580, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|Teutonicus|Teutōnicus||lang=la}}, from {{term|Teutones|Teutōnes|lang=la}}, {{term|Teutoni|Teutōnī|the Teutons|tr=name of a Germanic tribe that inhabited coastal Germany and devastated Gaul between 113-101 B.C.|lang=la}}. See {{term|Teuton|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˌtjuːˈtɒn.ɪk/}}, {{SAMPA|/%tju:"tQn.Ik/}}
*: {{rhymes|ɒnɪk}}

